## Findings
F1 (BLOCKING, high, crisis safety): the crisis escalation is dropped, with no log line, when the student's socket closes while the crisis flag write is in flight.
  - Code: apps/api/src/voice.ts onCrisisRecord (about lines 741-742): `if (!deps.escalateForTenant || text === undefined || text === "" || c.state === "closing" || c.state === "closed") return;`. `finalize` sets `c.state = "closing"` before it awaits `session.drain()`, which is what runs the queued crisis sink (flag write, then escalation), so any close that overlaps the crisis write silently skips the escalation.
  - Repro (my probe PB-C12c in qa/evidence/p1-u10-check-b/chkb-probe.test.ts; copy it to apps/api/tests and run `tsx --test tests/chkb-probe.test.ts`): slow the `student_flags` write, say the crisis phrase as an adult, `terminate()` the client socket while the write is held, release the write. Observed `{"flags":1,"escalations":0,"logs":[]}`; expected escalations 1 (or at least an operator log line). The flag row is stored, so the record survives, but the real-time counsellor channel (text-path parity, C12) gets nothing and nobody is told. A dropped call is among the likeliest things a student in crisis does.
  - Contrast: a graceful `end` right after the crisis sentence still escalates (PB-C12e passes), so the defect is confined to a close that races the write.
  - Why FAIL: C12 and the required hostile variant "crisis speech ... escalates" are not true for this input; the repair is one clause (probe R1) and no maker test depends on it.
F2 (non-blocking, low, liveness): when the NEWEST waiter dies while an older waiter still waits behind the same old session, the older waiter is told `superseded` and closed, leaving the student with no live session (probe PB-C10b: `{"cClosed":true,"cErrors":["superseded"],"live":0,"backends":1}`). `finalize` deletes `latestStart` for the dead newest start, so `latestStart.get(c.key) !== c` (voice.ts about line 987) is true for the survivor. No leak and nothing unsafe; the client reconnects. A one-condition fix is verified by probe R2 (`latestStart.has(c.key) && ...`).
F3 (non-blocking, low): an `escalateForTenant` factory that throws makes `onCrisisRecord` reject, which the live session reports to the student as `persist_failed`, and nothing is logged (probe PB-C12d `{"closed":false,"errors":["persist_failed"],"logs":[]}`). The session continues and the flag is stored. A misconfigured deployment would be invisible to operators.

PROPOSED-ISSUE: severity=high | unit=p1-u10-voice-ws | voice.ts onCrisisRecord drops the escalateForTenant call, silently, when c.state is closing/closed because the socket closed during the crisis flag write; the escalation must still run (it needs only claims, db and the redacted words) or a text-free voice_crisis_escalate_failed line must be logged. Repro PB-C12c.
PROPOSED-ISSUE: severity=low | unit=p1-u10-voice-ws | voice.ts handleStart step-aside test `latestStart.get(c.key) !== c` treats a vanished newest start as "superseded"; the older waiter should proceed when no newer start exists. Repro PB-C10b.
PROPOSED-ISSUE: severity=low | unit=p1-u10-voice-ws | voice.ts onCrisisRecord does not catch a throwing escalateForTenant factory (it is called outside crisisWrite): the student sees persist_failed and there is no operator log. Repro PB-C12d.

